  "comments": [
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " @target: es2015",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 18
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " The issue above, #49517, is fixed very indirectly. Here's some code",
      "start": 245,
      "end": 315
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " that shows the direct result of the change:",
      "start": 316,
      "end": 362
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " Ok",
      "start": 402,
      "end": 407
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " Error",
      "start": 446,
      "end": 454
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " Prev error, now ok",
      "start": 493,
      "end": 514
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " V[P] in `Nothing<V[P]>` is the substitution type `V[P] & Foo`. When",
      "start": 516,
      "end": 586
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " checking if that's assignable to `Foo` in the constraint of `Nothing`,",
      "start": 587,
      "end": 660
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " it passes the regular assignability check but then goes into intersection",
      "start": 661,
      "end": 737
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " property checks. To pull `foo` from the substitution type, it gets the",
      "start": 738,
      "end": 811
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " apparent type, which turns out to be something like `(Foo & Foo') | (Foo & Bar)`",
      "start": 812,
      "end": 895
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " where `Foo` and `Foo'` are different this-type instantiations of `Foo`.",
      "start": 896,
      "end": 970
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " Those two instantiations have the same `foo` property, but then `(Foo & Bar)['foo']`",
      "start": 971,
      "end": 1058
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " is a synthesized intersection property with a declaration in `Foo` and a",
      "start": 1059,
      "end": 1134
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " declaration in `Bar`. Because the former was marked as protected and the",
      "start": 1135,
      "end": 1210
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " latter was a different symbol, we previously thought the two symbols were",
      "start": 1211,
      "end": 1287
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " totally unrelated, as in `(Foo | Bar)['foo']`. The fix I implemented is to",
      "start": 1288,
      "end": 1365
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " check not that the two property symbols are identical, but that they share",
      "start": 1366,
      "end": 1443
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " some common declaration. The change is directly observable by seeing whether",
      "start": 1444,
      "end": 1523
    },
    {
      "type": "Line",
      "value": " `(Foo | (Foo & Bar))['foo']` is allowed.",
      "start": 1524,
      "end": 1567
    }
  ],
